# Tracer: builtin computation after checked object-definition unfolding.
#
# Before: the verifier computed the element but required the set argument to
# already be written as a StandardSet, so the final fact stayed unknown.
#
# have one Z = 1
# have integer_set set = Z
# one + 1 $in integer_set
#
# Former behavior: unknown because `integer_set` was not unfolded to `Z`.
#
# Now: unfold only checked `have x T = value` definitions, normalize the
# resolved fact to `2 $in Z`, compute it, normalize back to `1 + 1 $in Z`,
# and finally rewrite that proof back to this source goal.
have one Z = 1
have integer_set set = Z

one + 1 $in integer_set

# Current behavior: succeeds with the original fact as the result and exact
# defining-equality FactIds in its resolved-computation evidence.
#
# Boundary: replacing the second definition with `have unknown_set set` keeps
# `one + 1 $in unknown_set` unknown; no value or equality is invented.
#
# Evidence: target/release/litex -compact -runner -isolated -f examples/01_proof_patterns/resolved_builtin_computation.lit
